# Observability

Observability means understanding what is happening inside the app.

In a RAG app, many things can go wrong:

```text
PDF loading fails
Embedding fails
Retriever finds wrong chunks
LLM gives weak answer
Token cost becomes high
Response is slow
```

Observability helps us see and fix those problems.

## What To Track

Track requests:

```text
Which endpoint was called?
How long did it take?
Did it fail?
```

Track indexing:

```text
Which file was indexed?
How many chunks were created?
How long did indexing take?
Did embedding fail?
```

Track retrieval:

```text
Which chunks were returned?
Which sources were used?
What was the top score?
```

Track LLM usage:

```text
prompt tokens
completion tokens
total tokens
model name
latency
errors
```

Track user experience:

```text
slow answers
failed uploads
empty answers
common questions
```

## Simple Log Example

```js
{
  event: "chat_completed",
  question: "What is the salary of CX-MA-001?",
  sources: ["company x branch morocco, page 6"],
  promptTokens: 3201,
  completionTokens: 262,
  durationMs: 4500
}
```

## Why It Matters

Without observability, we guess.

With observability, we can answer:

```text
Why was the answer wrong?
Was retrieval bad?
Was the LLM slow?
Did token usage increase?
Which document caused an error?
```

## Simple Presentation Version

```text
Observability means tracking logs, errors, token usage, latency, retrieval sources, and indexing status so we can understand and improve the RAG app.
```

